  "final_output": "## Root cause\nThe cart v2.1.0 deploy at 09:40 UTC (\"Upgrade Redis client library\") is the cause. After the new Redis client library went live, cart write requests started to fail. The cart logs show \"add to cart failed\" with a Redis OOM error, and the new client probably keeps too much data in Redis. The Redis problem started after this change, and it is the latest change in the list.\n\n## Evidence\n- `ServiceErrorRateHigh` for cart (25.2%) at 11:15 UTC.\n- Cart error rate is up to about 39% in 11:00-12:00. Latency is normal.\n- New log pattern: \"add to cart failed\", error \"OOM command not allowed when used memory > 'maxmemory'\" (first at 11:10).\n- `list_changes` for cart shows the last change: deploy v2.1.0, \"Upgrade Redis client library\", at 09:40.\n- Cart errors per minute: average 0.02 before the deploy (09:00-09:40) and average 137 after it (09:40-12:00). The errors rose after the deploy.\n\n## Customer impact\nCustomers cannot add items to the cart from about 11:10 UTC. The error rate is about 39% for cart. I did not check checkout.\n\n## Next steps\nRoll back cart to v2.0.7. Then check that the cart error rate goes back to normal."
